  "bio": "Andrés Goens is Assistant Professor (W2-TT) at <a href=\"https://www.tu-darmstadt.de\">TU Darmstadt</a>. Before that, he was an Assistant Professor (UD) at the <a href=\"https://www.uva.nl/\">University of Amsterdam</a>. Before that, he was a Research Associate at the <a href=\"https://ed.ac.uk/\">University of Edinburgh</a> and at the <a href=\"https://www.barkhauseninstitut.org/\">Barkhausen Institut</a>. He received a Ph.D. (Dr.rer.nat.) degree (Hons.) in computer science from <a href=\"https://www.tu-dresden.de\">TU Dresden<a/> in Germany, and an M.Sc. degree in mathematics in from <a href=\"https://www.rwth-aachen.de\">RWTH Aachen University</a>, also in Germany.",
